{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_007 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, which substantially outperforms scgpt-based multiprofile models (0.514–0.530). The key remaining uncertainty is whether adding the image modality can further improve on this strong RNA signal, or whether it dilutes performance (as seen with scgpt, where multimodal 0.525 ≈ rna_only 0.530). Config_020 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the minimal single-variable extension of config_007: it keeps the same RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation, and only adds the image branch with weighted fusion. This cleanly isolates the contribution of the image modality under the best-performing RNA representation. Under a limited budget, resolving whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile with pca_n2000 is the highest-value question, as it determines whether subsequent experiments should invest in image-encoder upgrades or focus on RNA-side refinements."
}

